// Title: Suspicious Vsls-Agent Command With AgentExtensionPath Load
// Sigma ID: d13a374c-2ee8-4f30-b884-ff498947b927
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: bohops
// Date: 2022-10-30 | Modified: 2026-11-06
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects Microsoft Visual Studio vsls-agent.exe lolbin execution with a suspicious library load
//   using the --agentExtensionPath parameter
// False positives:
//   - False positives depend on custom use of vsls-agent.exe
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/bohops/status/1583916360404729857
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ebd26c2d9cd57dc9489faa1f1346577be9947747/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_vslsagent_agentextensionpath_load.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\vsls-agent.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "--agentExtensionPath") and (not(ProcessCommandLine contains "Microsoft.VisualStudio.LiveShare.Agent."))
